Consider the following C code that inserts a node at the **end** of a singly linked list. What is the time complexity of this insertion?

```c
void insertEnd(struct Node** head_ref, int data) {
    struct Node* new_node = malloc(sizeof(struct Node));
    new_node->data = data;
    new_node->next = NULL;
    if (*head_ref == NULL) { *head_ref = new_node; return; }
    struct Node* temp = *head_ref;
    while (temp->next != NULL)
        temp = temp->next;
    temp->next = new_node;
}
```

Analyze the following C code that attempts to delete a node with value `target` from a singly linked list. What is the bug in this code?

```c
void deleteNode(struct Node** head, int target) {
    struct Node* temp = *head;
    while (temp != NULL && temp->data != target)
        temp = temp->next;
    if (temp == NULL) return;
    temp->data = temp->next->data;
    temp->next = temp->next->next;
}
```

