**[HARD]** Consider the following C function that manipulates a non-empty singly linked list with at least 3 nodes.

```c
void mystery(struct Node** head) {
    struct Node *prev = NULL, *curr = *head, *next = NULL;
    while (curr != NULL) {
        next = curr->next;
        curr->next = prev;
        prev = curr;
        curr = next;
    }
    *head = prev;
}
```
If the original list is `1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5 -> NULL`, what is the state of the list after calling `mystery(&head)`? Also, how many pointer updates happen in total during the execution of this function?
